    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d957">

                <pb facs="0819" n="811" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg811"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.3394/251: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-02-12T16:00:00+09:00">February 12, 1937—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 12—4:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>54. Department’s 28, February 10, noon.<anchor n="25" xml:id="d957-f1"/> Foreign
                    Office has orally informed me today that Army and Navy have stated that <pb
                        facs="0820" n="812" xml:id="pg812"/> visits of <hi rendition="#italic">Gold
                        Star</hi> to Palau, Saipan and Truk would not be agreeable but visits to
                    Yokohama, Kobe and Miike would be agreeable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
